there, it could be a problem with the deployment configuration, like image pull failures, resource limits, or scheduling constraints. Alternatively, if the pod is listed but in a CrashLoopBackOff state, that would indicate an application error. \n\nBy checking the pods again, the user can confirm if the pod is being created and its current status. If the pod is in a CrashLoopBackOff state, they can then look into the logs or check the events for more details. If the pod isn\'t listed, the issue might be with the deployment configuration or the node where it\'s supposed to run. \n\nSo, the next tool call should be to get the list of pods again to verify their current state and identify any issues with the user-service pod.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -n social-network"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bdd097d5a88b722e', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 465, 'prompt_tokens': 4369, 'total_tokens': 4834, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcf0-7bd4-7e90-930b-e20ca52b1737-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -n social-network'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bdd097d5a88b722e', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4369, 'output_tokens': 465, 'total_tokens': 4834}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                                      READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\ncompose-post-service-886c98b48-bd7px      1/1     Running   0          2m38s\nhome-timeline-redis-5cdbd67f7c-8npbr      1/1     Running   0          2m38s\nhome-timeline-service-5d6bb5597d-kkqlk    1/1     Running   0          2m36s\njaeger-68c66