/1 containers ready. The previous attempt to get logs failed because the pod name might have changed or there was an error. Now that I know the pod is named user-service-746f96d8d6-fmppf, I should try getting its logs again. The logs will show any errors during startup. Also, checking the readiness probe configuration is important because if the probe is failing, the pod won\'t be marked as ready. The readiness probe is set to check http://:8080/healthz, so maybe the application isn\'t starting correctly or the health check endpoint is wrong. I should look into the logs to find out why the health check isn\'t passing. Another possibility is resource constraints, but since the pod is running, maybe it\'s a configuration issue. Let me check the logs first.\n</think>\n\nexec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \n"kubectl logs user-service-746f96d8d6-fmppf -n social-network"  \nThe user-service pod is in the "Running" state but not marked as ready. To diagnose the issue, I need to inspect the container logs to identify runtime errors, failed startup processes, or issues with the readiness probe (e.g., incorrect health check endpoint, application crashes, or configuration misloads). This will directly reveal the root cause of the pod\'s unavailability.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 303, 'prompt_tokens': 4540, 'total_tokens': 4843, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfcf0-941d-7c91-bff4-741bf05f92ac-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4540, 'output_tokens': 303, 'total_tokens': 4843}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='a9785b69-dcff-4aeb-bfd2-5f5b9711c2d6'), AIMessage(content='<t